    {
      "CN": "JAKO202505743301804",
      "DBCode": "JAKO",
      "Title": "Ligilactobacillus salivarius WB21의 구취 및 치주염에 대한 예방효과",
      "Title2": "Preventive effects of Ligilactobacillus salivarius WB21 on halitosis and periodontitis",
      "Abstract": "목적: 구취는 일반적으로 치주염 관련 세균에 의해 발생하는 불쾌한 냄새로 정의된다. Ligilactobacillus salivarius WB21은 사람 장에서 분리된 프로바이오틱스이다. 본 연구의 목적은 감수성 분석 및 공동 배양 시스템을 사용하여 치주 병원균에 대한 L. salivarius WB21의 항균 활성과 휘발성 황 화합물(VSC) 배출에 대한 WB21 균주의 억제 효과를 조사하는 것이다. 연구 재료 및 방법: 항균 활성은 감수성 분석 및 세균 배양액과 혼합 배양 시스템을 이용한 혼합조건을 사용하여 측정하였다. VSC의 수준은 가스 크로마토그래피로 측정하였다. 결과: L. salivarius WB21 균주의 배양되었던 배지 12.5% 농도 이상에서 Porphyromonas gingivalis, Tannerella forsythia 및 Treponema denticola의 성장을 유의하게 억제하였다(P < 0.05). 또한, L. salivarius WB21과 혼합 배양 시, 치주염관련 세균과 WB21종을 1 : 5 비율 이상의 환경에서 치주염 관련 세균의 성장이 유의하게 억제되었다(P < 0.05). L. salivarius WB21과 혼합 배양 시, 치주염 관련세균과 WB21종을 1 : 1 비율 이상의 환경에서 치주염 관련 세균이 생성하는 VSC 수치가 유의하게 감소하였다(P < 0.05). 결론: L. salivarius WB21은 치주염과 구취를 예방하는 프로바이오틱스 후보 물질이 될 수 있다고 사료된다.",
      "Abstract2": "Purpose: Halitosis is generally defined as an unpleasant odor and generated by periodontitis related bacteria. Ligilactobacillus salivarius WB21 is a probiotics isolated from the human intestine. The aim of present study was to investigate antimicrobial activity of L. salivarius WB21 against periodontopathogens using susceptibility assay and co-cultivation system and inhibitory effects the WB21 strain on emission of volatile sulfur compounds (VSCs). Materials and Methods: The antimicrobial activity was performed using susceptibility assay and co-cultivating condition with cell culture insert. The levels of VSCs were measured by a gas chromatograph. Results: The spent culture medium of WB21 strain significantly inhibited the growth of Porphyromonas gingivalis, Tannerella forsythia, and Treponema denticola at concentration of 12.5% or higher (P < 0.05). Also, the growth of the periodontitis related bacteria was significantly inhibited in co-cultivating with L. salivarius WB21 in condition of 1:5 ratio or higher (P < 0.05). In co-cultivation conditions with L. salivarius WB21, the levels of VSCs produced by periodontitis related bacteria were significantly decreased in mixed conditions of 1 : 1 ratio or higher (P < 0.05). Conclusion: L. salivarius WB21 may be a probiotics candidate to prevent periodontitis and halitosis.",
      "Keyword": [
        "프로바이오틱스",
        "구취",
        "치주염",
        "예방효과"
      ],
      "keyword_raw": "프로바이오틱스 . 구취 . 치주염 . 예방효과",
      "Keyword2": [
        "probiotics",
        "l",
        "salivarius wb21(ligilactobacillus salivarius wb21)",
        "halitosis",
        "periodontitis",
        "preventive effect"
      ],
      "keyword2_raw": "probiotics . L. salivarius WB21(Ligilactobacillus salivarius WB21) . halitosis . periodontitis . preventive effect",
      "ISSN": [
        "2384-4353",
        "2384-4272"
      ],
      "DOI": "https://doi.org/10.14368/jdras.2025.41.4.297",
      "Pubyear": 2025,
      "Pubdate": "20251130",
      "JournalName": "Journal of dental rehabilitation and applied science = 구강회복응용과학지",
      "Author": [
        "Hyon-Mo Ku",
        "Hyun-Jun Yoo"
      ],
      "references": [],
      "similar": []
    },
    {
      "CN": "JAKO202510554007218",
      "DBCode": "JAKO",
      "Title": "치과용 유니트 수관으로부터 분리된 세균의 바이오필름 형성 특징",
      "Title2": "Biofilm-forming properties of bacteria isolated from dental unit waterlines",
      "Abstract": "Objectives: The aim of this study was to identify and compare the properties associated with the biofilm-forming abilities of bacteria isolated from water in dental unit waterlines (DUWLs). Methods: Twelve bacterial strains isolated from the output water of DUWLs were cultured in 12-well plates containing polyurethane tubing and R2A medium. The amount of biofilm formed by each strain was evaluated. Based on the amount of biofilm formed, three strains were selected, and the level of adhesion was determined for each strain depending on the inoculation concentration and incubation time. In addition, adhesion inhibitors were identified in the three strains, and their hydrophobicity and extracellular polymeric substances (EPS) formation were compared. Results: Among the 12 strains, the highest levels of biofilm accumulation were seen in Cupriavidus pauculus HY12. C. pauculus HY12 showed higher levels of adhesion at lower bacterial concentrations and shorter incubation times than other strains. The adhesion of C. pauculus HY12 was inhibited by trypsin. Among the three isolates, hydrophobicity and EPS production were the highest in Acidovorax delafieldii HY1. Conclusions: The results of this study provide a basis for understanding the mechanism of DUWL biofilm formation and the development of methods to inhibit biofilm formation.",
      "Abstract2": null,
