    {
      "CN": "JAKO202524857637419",
      "DBCode": "JAKO",
      "Title": "전라남도 고흥지역 스마트농업 부산물 자원순환을 위한 최적 입지 선정",
      "Title2": "Optimizing the Location for Biomass Resource Circulation from Smart Agriculture: A Case of Goheung, Jeollanam-do",
      "Abstract": "The increased use of fossil fuels has resulted in greenhouse gas emissions and various forms of environmental pollution. In response, there is a growing global interest in and research on renewable energy sources that can serve as alternatives to fossil fuels. This study focuses on selecting sites for bioenergy production facilities that utilize rice straw, an agricultural by-product, as a renewable energy source. Site analysis was performed using ArcGIS software. In the case study area of Goheung, paddy field locations were extracted from 1:5,000 scale digital maps provided by the National Geographic Information Institute and divided into 1 km<sup>2</sup> units. The centroid of each unit was assumed to be the focal point of rice straw production. Based on annual rice straw production, processing capacities of 20,000, 40,000, and 60,000 tons were evaluated, resulting in the identification of 1 to 3 potential sites for bioenergy production facilities. The estimated cost of rice straw raw material per liter of bioethanol was 545 KRW, 548 KRW, and 570 KRW for the 20,000, 40,000, and 60,000-ton collection scenarios, respectively. Consequently, the number of suitable biorefinery sites was determined to be 3, 1, and 1 for processing capacities of 20,000, 40,000, and 60,000 tons, respectively.",
      "Abstract2": null,
