    {
      "CN": "DIKO0014012343",
      "DBCode": "DIKO",
      "Title": "콜레스테롤 골격을 기반으로 하는 양이온성 리피드의 구조에 따른 트랜스펙션 효율에 대한 연구",
      "Title2": "The study of transfection efficiency on the structure of cholesterol based cationic lipids",
      "Abstract": "In this study, various cholesterol derivatives were synthesized and tested their gene transfer efficiency, size, zeta potential, fluorescence, cytotoxicity, and structure. There was no correlation between transfer efficiency and physico-chemical properties, but transfection efficiencies were determined mainly by cell type. There are many people who were sick with cardiovascular disorders, nerve disorder, and hereditary problems. These diseases cannot be treated completely by conventional drugs, so gene therapy will be a powerful solution. In this remedy, carriers were classified as virus, non-virus vector Non-virus vector has relatively low efficiency compared to viral vectors, but it is safe, easy to modify. Using variable cationic lipids based on cholesterol, which was proved to have stability in serum, many lipoplexes were formed with DOPE, DNA. In AGS cell line, lipid C was excellent effect than commercial lipids – LF, LFA, DP and DC-chol. Lipids B and D showedcomparable efficiency at Huh-7 cell line even with serum. Lipid A which had cabamoyl group linkage did not show effective transfection efficiency than lipid B-D having ether group. If the chain have side bond – isopropyl, multiple bond, transfection efficiency was decreased. Chol-THEA was synthesized with lipid B. It was substituted amine to tri-hydroxyethylamine head. This lipid has 3 time higher transfection efficiency than LFA at Huh-7 cell line, but there were no significant effect at COS7, MCF-7. To investigate the role of lipid composition in transfection efficiency, DOTAP/DOPE liposome was formed withvarious concentrations and compositions. There were no relationshipsamong size, zeta potential, lipid composition, structure of lipoplex and transfection efficiency. Mainly cell type determines transfection efficiency. In summary, various kinds of cholesterol based cationic lipids were newly synthesized and the relationship of the transfection efficiency physico-chemical property was investigated. Some novel cationic lipids showed superior transfection efficiency compared to commercial lipids. Among various factors related in transfection efficiency, cell type was revealed as most influencing determinants.",
