    {
      "CN": "DIKO0017276382",
      "DBCode": "DIKO",
      "Title": "Polylactic acid(PLA)및 천연섬유를 적용한 바이오 기반 복합소재의 기계적 특성 연구",
      "Title2": null,
      "Abstract": "Environmental concerns regarding conventional polymers have driven the adoption of biodegradable materials, among which polylactic acid (PLA) stands out for its biodegradability, compostability, and relatively good mechanical properties. However, PLA suffers from brittleness, low flexibility, and limited impact resistance, which restricts its use in high-performance applications. This study addresses these limitations by incorporating natural fibers and a bio-based plasticizer to enhance the mechanical properties of PLA-based composites. &#xD; Jute fibers were selected as reinforcement for their low cost, high specific strength, and renewability. To overcome poor interfacial adhesion caused by the hydrophilic nature of jute, fibers were chemically modified through oxidation followed by imination using amines (DDA, HA, Priamine) to increase surface hydrophobicity. PLAbased composites were fabricated via solvent casting to ensure uniform dispersion of fibers and additives. Surface modification was confirmed using FT-IR, SEM, and contact angle analysis, whereas tensile properties were measured using a universal testing machine (UTM).&#xD; Neat PLA exhibited tensile strengths of 18–24 MPa, with the highest value (23.9 MPa) observed for PLA-18. Adding Priamine significantly improved ductility, with an elongation at break of 10.3% at 7.5 phr while maintaining tensile strength. Composites reinforced with hexylaminemodified jute (OJ-HA) at 2 phr showed the best performance, with 30.4 MPa tensile strength and 3.2% elongation—approximately 40% higher than neat PLA. Glass fiber (10 phr) and carbon fiber (5 phr) composites achieved tensile strengths of 30.2 MPa and 35.6 MPa, respectively, indicating that modified natural fibers can deliver mechanical properties comparable to synthetic fibers. In conclusion, combining bio-based polymers, modified natural fibers, and ecofriendly plasticizers provides an effective strategy for developing sustainable, high-performance composites and indicates strong potential for industrial applications.",
      "Abstract2": null,
      "Keyword": [
        "바이오 기반 복합소재",
        "천연섬유"
      ],
