    {
      "CN": "DIKO0017166997",
      "DBCode": "DIKO",
      "Title": "홍삼과 노루궁뎅이버섯 복합추출물이 면역기능의 활성에 미치는 영향",
      "Title2": null,
      "Abstract": "This study evaluated the immunomodulatory and anti-inflammatory effects of a combined extract of red ginseng and Hericium erinaceus (RHM) by analyzing cytokine secretion and the expression of key immune-related genes in Balb/c mice splenocytes and lung cells. Cytokine analysis revealed that RHM extract significantly increased the production of IL-2, IL-4, IL-12, and IFN-γ, particularly at higher concentrations (400 μg/mL), compared to RGE extract alone. Gene expression analysis demonstrated that RHM significantly suppressed the expression of mMUC5AC, a mucin-related gene, and mTARC, a chemokine involved in allergic inflammation, indicating its potential in mitigating excessive mucus production and immune cell recruitment. Additionally, RHM showed a strong inhibitory effect on mCOX-2, a key gene in inflammatory pathways, while no significant differences were observed in mMIP2 and mTRPA1 expression levels. mTRPV1, which plays a role in pain and inflammation, was notably suppressed in the red ginseng treated group, highlighting the differential effects of red ginseng and RHM. These results suggest that the synergistic effects of red ginseng and RHM enhance both innate and adaptive immune responses, while also offering potential benefits in inflammation regulation. The combined extract shows promise as a natural agent for immune modulation and inflammatory control, with RHM contributing significantly to its efficacy. Further studies are warranted to elucidate the detailed mechanisms, long-term safety, and clinical applicability of this combined extract.",
      "Abstract2": null,
      "Keyword": [
        "노루궁뎅이버섯 홍삼 면역체계 사이토카인 발현 염증 조절 유전자 발현 분석"
