      "Title": "Oligonucleotide-mixed micelles with amphiphilic peptide and drug for the treatment of acute lung injury",
      "Title2": null,
      "Abstract": "Acute lung injury (ALI) is a representative inflammatory phenomenon in the lung. For treatment of this disease, therapeutic gene delivery could be the method. To reduce the pro-inflammatory cytokine level of the lung, ternary micelle was designed which can target microRNA155 (miR155). miR155 contributes to the increase of inflammatory cytokine by targeting SOCS1, which is the important suppressor of cytokine signaling pathway. To suppress miR155, antagonist sequence of miR155 (AMO155) was used, and cholesterol was attached to AMO155 to make micelle in aqueous solution itself. For more high delivery efficiency, R3V6 peptide and GA were also added to the micelles. R3V6 peptide could improve gene delivery efficiency, and GA has anti-inflammatory effects. These three substrates have characteristic of micelle structure in aqueous solution, so it could mix into one by using hydrophobic interaction. The ternary micelle, AMO155c/[R3V6/GA] had highest delivery efficiency, anti-inflammatory effect, and it could block miR155 pathway by checking SOCS1 signal. Furthermore, the infiltration of monocytes into the lungs were more inhibited by ternary micelle than single, dual micelles. Due to these delivery efficiency and effectiveness, AMO155c/[R3V6/GA] ternary micelles could be useful for treatment of ALI.",
