    {
      "CN": "NART136155866",
      "DBCode": "JAFO",
      "Title": "免疫检查点抑制剂治疗相关垂体炎1例并文献复习（英文）",
      "Title2": "Hypophysitis associated with immune check piont inhibotors treatment: A case report and literature review",
      "Abstract": "<P>We reported a case of secondary adrenal insufficiency caused by programmed death 1 (PD-1) inhibitor. A 65-year-old patient received immunotherapy for right lung squamous cell carcinoma invading the chest wall (cT4N2M0) for 4 times. Two weeks after the last immunotherapy, he developed anorexia and fatigue, and was admitted to our hospital with severe hyponatremia. After further examination, the patient was diagnosed with PD-1 inhibitor related hypophysitis and secondary adrenal insufficiency. After glucocorticoid supplementation, the patient’s clinical symptoms were significantly improved. It is recommended that patients receiving immune check piont inhibotors should be asked in detail about their medical history before initiating treatment, baseline screening should be carried out reasonably, and regular follow-up about endocrine gland hormone and related biochemical indexes after treatment should be carried out. Meanwhile, pay attention to the related symptoms and signs of patients in order to find endocrine gland adverse reactions in time.</P>",
      "Abstract2": null,
      "Keyword": [],
      "keyword_raw": "免疫&#x68c0;&#x67e5;点抑制&#x5242;. PD-1抑制&#x5242;. &#x7ee7;&#x53d1;性&#x80be;上腺皮&#x8d28;功能&#x51cf;退 . Immune check piont inhibotors . Programmed death-1inhibitor . Secondary adrenal insufficiency;",
