    {
      "CN": "NART136115925",
      "DBCode": "JAFO",
      "Title": "铁死亡与肿瘤免疫",
      "Title2": "Ferroptosis and tumor immunity",
      "Abstract": "<P>Ferroptosis is a unique form of cell death driven by iron-dependent lipid peroxidation, with regulatory mechanisms involving metabolic dysregulation and imbalance in redox systems. Ferroptosis is closely related to various immune cells in the tumor immune microenvironment, including both anti-tumor and pro-tumor immune cells, and it demonstrates significant potential in tumor immunotherapy. A systematic review of the regulatory mechanisms of ferroptosis and its relationship with immune cells can provide deeper insights into its application prospects in tumor immunotherapy.</P>",
      "Abstract2": null,
      "Keyword": [],
      "keyword_raw": "&#x94c1;死亡 . 免疫&#x7ec6;胞 . &#x80bf;瘤免疫治&#x7597;. ferroptosis . immune cells . tumor immunotherapy;",
      "Keyword2": [
        "ferroptosis",
        "immune cells",
        "tumor immunotherapy"
      ],
      "keyword2_raw": null,
